.TH JALA 1 "October 2026" "jala 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jala \- display a Persian (Jalali) calendar in the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jala
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIMONTH\fR] [\fIYEAR\fR]
.br
.B jala
.B \-c
\fIDATE\fR
.br
.B jala
.B \-d
\fIDATE1 DATE2\fR
.br
.B jala
.B \-t
[\fI+FORMAT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jala
is a small command-line program that prints the Persian (Jalali)
calendar in the terminal, closely modeled after
.BR jcal (1)
and
.BR jdate (1).
It can display a single month, three consecutive months, or a full
year; it can highlight today, mark Fridays, render Persian digits
and month names, show the day-of-year, use the Imperial
(Shahanshahi) year, convert dates between the Jalali and Gregorian
calendars, compute the difference between two dates, and highlight
Iranian official holidays from an embedded dataset.
.PP
The Gregorian-to-Jalali conversion is implemented with the standard
JDN (Julian Day Number) algorithm and is accurate across the entire
supported range (years 1 to 9999).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y
Print the full year as a 3 columns \(mu 4 rows grid.
.TP
.BR \-3
Print three months side by side: the previous month, the current
(or requested) month, and the next month.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stacked
Print months in a single column instead of side by side. Useful
with
.B \-3
or
.B \-y
when the terminal is narrow.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-persian
Render digits and month/weekday names in Persian. Each weekday
header cell is wrapped in Unicode LRM (Left-to-Right Mark) so the
column stays left-to-right regardless of the terminal's bidi
handling.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-english
Print three-letter English weekday abbreviations
.RB ( Sat ", " Sun ", " Mon ", " Tue ", " Wed ", " Thu ", " Fri )
instead of the short
.BR Sh/Ye/Do
form.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-julian
Show the day-of-year (1 to 365 or 366) instead of the day-of-month.
In this mode each cell is widened to three columns.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-pahlavi
Display the year using the Imperial (Shahanshahi) epoch, whose
origin is the coronation of Cyrus the Great in 559 BC.
The formula is
.IR "Imperial year = Jalali year + 1180" .
A
.B (pa)
label is appended to the year in the header.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-convert " " \fIDATE\fR
Convert
.I DATE
between the Jalali and Gregorian calendars and print both.
If the year part is less than 1700 the input is treated as Jalali;
otherwise it is treated as Gregorian.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-diff " " \fIDATE1 DATE2\fR
Print the number of days between
.I DATE1
and
.IR DATE2 .
When the difference is seven days or more, the result is also shown
as a whole number of weeks plus the remaining days.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-today " " [\fI+FORMAT\fR]
Print the current date and time and exit. If
.I +FORMAT
is given, it is interpreted like the GNU
.BR date (1)
format string (see
.B "FORMAT SPECIFIERS"
below). The leading
.B +
is optional.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-no-bidi
Do not wrap Persian weekday cells in the Unicode LRM marker. Use
this on terminals that render the marker as a visible control
character or that otherwise mishandle bidi controls.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-no-holidays
Do not highlight Iranian official holidays. By default, days listed
in the embedded holiday dataset are printed in red.
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-events
After printing the calendar, list every event recorded for the
displayed range, one per line. Holidays are shown in red, other
events in cyan. Combine with
.B \-p
for Persian digits and with
.B \-n
to disable color.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-nocolor
Disable ANSI color output. Useful when piping the output to a file
or another program.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH "DATE FORMATS"
Dates are accepted in either of the following forms:
.PP
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
.IB YYYY / MM / DD
.IP \(bu 2
.IB YYYY \- MM \- DD
.IP \(bu 2
.B today
or
.B now
.RE
.PP
A year less than 1700 is interpreted as a Jalali year; a year
greater than or equal to 1700 is interpreted as a Gregorian year.
This heuristic works for all practical dates but can be overridden
by writing the year in full.
.SH "FORMAT SPECIFIERS"
The
.B \-t
option accepts the following conversion specifiers in its format
string. The list mirrors the subset of GNU
.BR date (1)
that is meaningful for a Jalali calendar.
.TP
.B %Y
Four-digit year (Jalali, or Imperial if
.B \-P
is set).
.TP
.B %y
Two-digit year.
.TP
.B %m
Two-digit month (01 to 12).
.TP
.B %d
Two-digit day of month (01 to 31).
.TP
.B %B
Full month name (for example
.IR Mehr ).
.TP
.B %b
Three-letter month name.
.TP
.B %A
Full weekday name (for example
.IR Sunday
or
.IR "یکشنبه" ).
.TP
.B %a
Short weekday name (for example
.IR Sun
or
.IR ی ).
.TP
.B %H
Hour (00 to 23).
.TP
.B %M
Minute (00 to 59).
.TP
.B %S
Second (00 to 59).
.TP
.B %%
A literal percent sign.
.TP
.B %n
A newline.
.TP
.B %t
A tab.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B jala
Show the current month.
.TP
.B jala 7 1405
Show Mehr 1405.
.TP
.B jala \-3 7 1405
Show Shahrivar, Mehr, and Aban of 1405 side by side.
.TP
.B jala \-ys 1405
Show all twelve months of 1405 in a single column.
.TP
.B jala \-p
Show the current month with Persian digits and names.
.TP
.B jala \-e
Show the current month with English weekday abbreviations.
.TP
.B jala \-j 7 1405
Show Mehr 1405 with the day-of-year instead of the day-of-month.
.TP
.B jala \-P 7 1405
Show Mehr 1405 using the Imperial year (2585).
.TP
.B jala \-t
Print the current date and time.
.TP
.B jala \-tp '+%A %d %B %Y'
Print the current date with Persian names, for example
.IR "یکشنبه ۱۲ مهر ۱۴۰۵" .
.TP
.B jala \-E 1 1405
Show Farvardin 1405 and list every event recorded in that month.
.TP
.B jala \-H 1 1405
Show Farvardin 1405 without highlighting official holidays.
.TP
.B jala \-B \-p
Show the current month in Persian, without LRM wrapping around the
weekday header. Useful on terminals that render LRM visibly.
.TP
.B jala \-c 1405/07/12
Convert 1405/07/12 (Jalali) to Gregorian.
.TP
.B jala \-c 2026-10-04
Convert 2026-10-04 (Gregorian) to Jalali.
.TP
.B jala \-d 1405/07/12 today
Print how many days ago 1405/07/12 was.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid input (bad month, bad year, unparsable date, or a
.B \-d
invocation with fewer than two dates).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to any non-empty value, color output is disabled, matching
the informal
.B NO_COLOR
convention.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/bin/jala
The executable.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR jcal (1),
.BR jdate (1),
.BR cal (1),
.BR date (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Mahdi Moradi.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at the project's issue tracker.
.PP
Holiday and event data is sourced from
.UR https://github.com/hasan-ahani/shamsi-holidays
hasan-ahani/shamsi-holidays
.UE
(MIT License) and embedded at build time. Updates require a new
release of
.BR jala .
.PP
Persian text alignment in the terminal depends on the font and on
the terminal's support for bidi control characters. If the weekday
header appears reversed, try a terminal that supports LRM (for
example, recent versions of GNOME Terminal, Konsole, or Alacritty),
or pass
.B \-B
to disable the marker.